    "notes": [
      "$or is a Boolean Expression operator used in aggregation expressions",
      "Returns true if ANY expression evaluates to true (short-circuits on first true)",
      "Empty array [] returns false",
      "Truthy values: non-zero numbers, non-empty strings, arrays (even empty), objects, true, ObjectId, Date, Timestamp, Binary data",
      "Falsy values: 0, 0.0, empty string \"\", null, undefined, false",
      "Non-array input throws TypeMismatch error",
      "Can be combined with $and, $not, $cond, $switch, $filter, $eq",
      "Short-circuits - stops evaluating after finding first truthy value",
      "Extracted from MongoDB jstests: not.js, cond.js, filter.js, collation_expressions.js",
      "Implementation tested in evaluate_or_test.cpp"
    ],
